@@ -14,4 +14,17 @@ wrong. A refused change leaves the list as it was.
 - A priority is `low`, `normal` or `high`; a task without one is `normal`.
 - A tag cannot be empty and cannot contain a space (any whitespace counts as a space).
 
+## Bulk import
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` adds many tasks at once, for teams moving their lists over from spreadsheets. The
+text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`:
+
+- The priority may be left empty for `normal`, and is otherwise one of the priorities above.
+- The tags are separated by spaces, for example `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`.
+- Blank lines are skipped. A semicolon ends the title, so a title cannot contain one.
+
+Every valid line is added, even when others are refused. The call returns `{ imported, rejected }`:
+`imported` is how many tasks were added, and `rejected` lists each refused line as `{ line, reason }`,
+where `line` counts from 1, blank lines included, so it points at the same place in the text.
+
 Run its tests with `npm test`.
